{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_11_scale_program_block_table_zone", "label": "Block / Table / Zone is the editable unit above rooftop scale", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/11-scale-program.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The one structural decision that makes 100 MW possible \u2014 it is the industry paradigm, and scaling per-panel raycast with a BVH alone was rejected because it removes the O(n\u00b2) but still stores, edits and re-shades 150k objects: wrong abstraction, not a performance bug."}, {"id": "docs_11_scale_program_three_regimes", "label": "Three Scale Regimes (rooftop / large C&I / utility)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/11-scale-program.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Regime is a property of the design, not the tenant \u2014 a 100 kW rooftop and a 40 MW park coexist in one tenant, and the studio switches paradigm at the block boundary."}, {"id": "docs_11_scale_program_poc_cliffs", "label": "The Five Documented POC Cliffs", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/11-scale-program.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_11_scale_program_phase_a", "label": "Scale Phase A (BVH, ProjectionContext, worker chunking, blocks schema)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/11-scale-program.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Splits three ways \u2014 context injection and the blocks schema land at port time, BVH plus far-cap removal land immediately post-port as separate golden-verified changes, and GPU shading is Phase B, not A."}, {"id": "docs_11_scale_program_phase_b", "label": "Scale Phase B \u2014 Large C&I (block editing, GPU shading, server sims, LOD)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/11-scale-program.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_11_scale_program_phase_c", "label": "Scale Phase C \u2014 Utility (trackers, DEM terrain, block electrical, DXF)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/11-scale-program.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_11_scale_program_gpu_shadow_map", "label": "GPU Shadow-Map Shading (288 sun-sample depth maps)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/11-scale-program.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The published solar-cadaster technique: depth-map testing is far cheaper than ray intersection. GPU and CPU paths are pinned against each other by a \u00b12% tolerance test \u2014 one SHADING_ENGINE_VERSION, two executors."}, {"id": "docs_11_scale_program_tracker_backtracking", "label": "Single-Axis Tracker GCR Backtracking", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/11-scale-program.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Closed-form calculation mirroring pvlib's tracking.singleaxis, validated against pvlib reference vectors as a golden-file test; the 288-sample quadrature and depth-map path are unchanged \u2014 only instance matrices move."}, {"id": "docs_11_scale_program_dem_terrain", "label": "GLO-30 DEM Terrain + terrain-aware row spacing", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/11-scale-program.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Closes the POC's deferred cliff exactly where its comment said 'real math and is deferred rather than approximated' \u2014 pitch per block computed from the block's fitted plane."}, {"id": "docs_11_scale_program_performance_budgets", "label": "Performance Budgets per Regime (release criteria)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/11-scale-program.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A phase does not ship over budget; the block/table model keeps the utility column honest because 175k modules is ~4,000 tables, so the persisted and edited object count stays in the thousands at every regime."}, {"id": "docs_11_scale_program_deferrals", "label": "Explicit Deferrals with Re-evaluation Triggers", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/11-scale-program.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Each deferral names the measurable condition that reopens it \u2014 terrain-following articulation, a server GPU farm, a Rust/WASM kernel, utility autorouting and WebXR are deferred with stated triggers rather than vague 'later'."}, {"id": "docs_11_scale_program_honesty_at_scale", "label": "The Honesty Rule at Scale", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/11-scale-program.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Scale changes resolution, never honesty: provenance goes block-level with an aggregate inheriting the weakest tier of its members, the shading model's documented limits stay printed, and there is no express lane for money staleness during long recomputes."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_11_scale_program_block_table_zone", "target": "docs_11_scale_program_three_regimes", "relation": "rationale_for", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/11-scale-program.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_11_scale_program_poc_cliffs", "target": "docs_11_scale_program_phase_a", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/11-scale-program.md", "so